---
title: "K1 Intelligence Module — Complete Architecture with Event & Message Flows"
description: |
  K1 production-ready agentic orchestrator kernel with full event flows, message passing, and K0 integration.

  Architecture: 5-layer microkernel | 70+ modules | 652 ADRs

  LAYER 1 (INPUT): 5 modules | 91 ADRs | <10ms P95
  - stream_switch: Audio/Text/Vision routing, 3 concurrent streams
  - operators: VAD <20ms, ASR <80ms, TTS <300ms
  - intent_router: 3-tier (rules 10ms, SLM 30ms, LLM 40ms)
  - meta_policy: Proactive suggestions, context-aware routing
  - sensors: BLE proximity, PIR motion, mmWave radar (ambient awareness)

  LAYER 2 (ORCHESTRATION): 3 modules | 127 ADRs | <100ms P95
  - planner: 4-stage (Sketch→Expand→Validate→Commit) <50ms
  - orchestrator: 3-phase (Negotiation→Selection→Execution) <250ms
  - protocol_monitor: 6 MPST protocols, FSM validation

  LAYER 3 (EXECUTION): 24 modules | 115 ADRs | Varies
  - agents: 8 agents (Concierge, Planner, Researcher, Tool Specialist, Safety Watch, etc.)
  - model_hub: 7 modules (registry, router, thermal, cache, provider, session, guard)
  - tools: 5 modules (registry, executor, sandbox, schema, feedback)
  - dialogue: 4 modules (manager, context, clarification, history)

  LAYER 4 (RUNTIME): 11 modules | 154 ADRs | <1ms P95
  - session_state: 6 sections (beliefs, scoreboard, control, persona, multimodal, meta)
  - actor_fabric: MPSC mailbox, 4-tier priority, supervisor trees
  - api_gateway: REST/GraphQL/gRPC, rate limiting, auth
  - voice_pipeline: Multi-device, echo cancellation, barge-in
  - learning: Feedback signals, drift detection, hot-reload
  - hitl: Human-in-the-Loop (5 protocols: step-by-step, RED band, nested, proactive)
  - intent_switch: Context-switch detection, 3-level intent drift taxonomy
  - kv_cache: Adaptive cache management, dynamic placement, hot/cold eviction, ZSTD compression
  - sync: Multi-device CRDT synchronization, hybrid LAN/Internet routing
  - protocol_monitor: Runtime FSM validation instance (6 protocols)
  - learning: Expanded with feedback signals, drift detection, hot-reload

  LAYER 5 (INFRASTRUCTURE): 8 modules | 165 ADRs | <5ms P95
  - bridge_k0: 6 ports (Command:5200, Query:5201, SSE:5202, Observability:5203, Health:5204, Arbitration:5205)
  - event_bus: Pub/sub <5ms, 17+ event types, backpressure
  - resilience: Circuit breaker, retry, timeout, bulkhead
  - thermal: 4-tier placement (Arctic→Cold→Warm→Hot)
  - observability: Metrics, tracing, logging (Prometheus, OTLP, structlog)
  - config: YAML configuration + environment variables
  - extensions: Plugin system (load/unload, isolation, manifest validation)
  - connectors: External system integration (API, DB, Message queue)

  EVENT FLOWS:
  - L1→L2: EventBus (INTENT_DETECTED, USER_INPUT, VOICE_COMMAND, BARGE_IN, SENSOR_EVENT)
  - L2→L3: Actor Mailbox (TaskAnnouncement→Proposal→Selection→TaskAssignment)
  - L3→L4: State Updates (BeliefUpdate, ScoreUpdate, ToolResult, CacheUpdate)
  - L2/L3/L4→K0: Bridge (Commands, Queries, SSE events, Metrics, Arbitration)
  - L4→L5: HITL Approvals, Intent Switches, Multi-device Sync, Protocol Violations

  PERFORMANCE: Hot path 135ms P95 | TTFT 150ms | E2E 2000ms | Memory 500MB

  PATTERNS: Actor Model (Hewitt 1973), MPST (Honda 2008), Capabilities (Dennis 1966),
           SEDA (Welsh 2001), Saga (Garcia-Molina 1987), Contract Net (Smith 1980),
           CRDT (Shapiro 2011), HITL (Amershi 2014)

author: "K1 Architecture Team"
version: "3.0.0"
---
